### Commented entries have reasonable defaults.
### Uncomment to edit them.
# Source: <source package name; defaults to package name>
Section: java
Priority: optional
Standards-Version: 3.9.2

Package: openjdk-8-jre-headless
Version: 999:0-equivs-stub
Maintainer: conmilo <noreply@github.com>
Provides: java-runtime-headless, java8-runtime-headless, java2-runtime-headless, java-virtual-machine, java-runtime, java8-runtime, java2-runtime
Architecture: amd64
Description: openjdk-8-jre-headless equivs stub for UniFi Video .deb
 Zero-file metapackage that satisfies the openjdk-8-jre-headless
 dependency of the UniFi Video controller .deb without actually
 installing any Java files. The "999:0-equivs-stub" epoch version
 is deliberately distinct from any real upstream package version
 so a future `dpkg -l openjdk-8-jre-headless` clearly indicates
 the stub vs. the real thing, and so we never accidentally collide
 with whatever version Ubuntu happens to ship (the previous stub
 version "8u492-1" matched Ubuntu noble's package exactly, which
 made apt think the real thing was already installed).
 .
 The real Java runtime (Canonical OpenJDK 21 LTS, since v3.10.13-13;
 earlier releases pinned AdoptOpenJDK 8u265-b01 -- see CHANGELOG
 v3.10.13-4 and v3.10.13-13 for the history) is shipped via apt's
 openjdk-21-jre-headless to /usr/lib/jvm/java-21-openjdk-amd64
 and is on the default PATH via the JAVA_HOME environment variable.
 This stub continues to exist because the UniFi Video .deb's
 Depends: line still names openjdk-8-jre-headless explicitly.
